    <string name="readmore"><u>Read More</u></string>
    <string name="rm1">To formally challenge a provider’s performance claims, you need to take several measurements within a geographic area and submit them to the FCC, the U.S. government agency that regulates telecommunications.</string>
    <string name="rm1b">Our app helps consumers take these measurements and automatically submits them to the FCC.</string>
    <string name="rm2">A challenge to a provider’s coverage claims is specific to a geographic area. The FCC has used a hexagonal tiling system to define regions. By collecting several measurements within one hexagonal region, a consumer can prove that the region does not have good mobile Internet performance, despite what their cell carrier may claim.</string>
    <string name="rm3">Our app shows two layers of hexagonal regions: a larger hexagonal region which contains seven (7) child hexagons.</string>
    <string name="rm3b">Challenges are for the larger hexagons, and you must take measurements within a specific number of child hexagons to count as a challenge.</string>

